## What it is

{{ repo_name }} is set up from the shared standard in [`.github`](https://github.com/JonathanTSilva/.github), so CI, hooks, dependency updates and agent instructions work like in the other repositories of JonathanTSilva.

## Quick start

{% if stack == 'python' %}
```sh
git clone https://github.com/{{ repo }}.git
cd {{ repo_name }}
uv sync
uv run pytest
```
{% elif stack == 'node' %}
```sh
git clone https://github.com/{{ repo }}.git
cd {{ repo_name }}
pnpm install
pnpm run test
```
{% elif stack == 'shell' %}
```sh
git clone https://github.com/{{ repo }}.git
cd {{ repo_name }}
```

Needs `shellcheck`, `shfmt` and `bats` for the checks.
{% elif stack == 'go' %}
```sh
git clone https://github.com/{{ repo }}.git
cd {{ repo_name }}
go test ./...
```
{% elif stack == 'rust' %}
```sh
git clone https://github.com/{{ repo }}.git
cd {{ repo_name }}
cargo test
```
{% elif stack == 'c-cpp' %}
```sh
git clone https://github.com/{{ repo }}.git
cd {{ repo_name }}
cmake -S . -B build
cmake --build build
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
```

Needs `cmake` and a C++ compiler.
{% elif stack == 'latex' %}
```sh
git clone https://github.com/{{ repo }}.git
cd {{ repo_name }}
latexmk -pdf -outdir=build main.tex
```

Needs `latexmk` and a TeX Live distribution.
{% else %}
```sh
git clone https://github.com/{{ repo }}.git
cd {{ repo_name }}
```
{% endif %}

Or open it in a dev container or GitHub Codespaces.

